    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented duplicate-email rejection for owner creation, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `RequireUniqueTelephone` rule).\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception carrying the offending normalized email.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds **409 Conflict** with `{\"errors\": [\"email\"]}`, matching the sibling telephone/household handlers.\n- `rest/function/owner/RequireUniqueEmail.java` \u2014 after email normalization, skips blank (optional) emails, then compares the lower-cased email against every existing owner via the shared `EmailNormalizer`, throwing when another owner already uses it.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Inserted a `uniqueEmail` step into `owners.POST.yml` immediately after the `email` (`NormalizeOwnerEmail`) step, so the check runs against the already-lower-cased value and before the record is persisted.\n\nThe `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test (create owner A with an email, then owner B reusing it \u2192 expects 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
